2. PROPOSED SOLUTION: HREWS OVERVIEW
=============================================================================

COMPONENTS:

A) Predictive Engine (Backend)
   Input: Patient data at discharge (age, medications, visits, LOS, diagnosis)
   Process: Logistic regression model (trained on 80K+ hospital discharges)
   Output: Readmission risk probability (0-100%)
   Timing: Automated calculation at discharge, updates if patient returns

B) Risk Stratification Module
   Input: Risk probability from engine
   Process: Categorize into Low/Moderate/High tiers
   Output: Risk tier assignment with key drivers

C) Intervention Protocols (Evidence-Based)
   
   LOW RISK (<8% probability):
   - Standard discharge summary
   - Routine follow-up appointment (2-4 weeks)
   - Written patient education materials
   - Assumption: Minimal intervention needed
   - Estimated cost per patient: $0 (standard care)
   
   MODERATE RISK (8-15% probability):
   - Enhanced discharge summary (standardized checklist)
   - Pharmacist medication reconciliation review
   - Nurse-led telephone follow-up (48-72 hours post-discharge)
   - Written instructions sent to primary care physician
   - Social work consult if social barriers identified
   - Estimated cost per patient: $250-500
   
   HIGH RISK (>15% probability):
   - Multidisciplinary discharge planning (physician, nurse, social worker, case manager)
   - In-home or telehealth nursing visit (within 48 hours)
   - Intensive medication reconciliation
   - Social work assessment for housing, food insecurity, transportation
   - Specialty follow-up appointment scheduled before discharge
   - Durable medical equipment arranged
   - Estimated cost per patient: $1,000-2,000

D) Clinical Dashboard (Frontend)
   
   For Discharge Planners:
   - Patient list with risk scores
   - Color-coded alerts (Green=Low, Yellow=Moderate, Red=High)
   - Recommended intervention checklist by risk tier
   - Clinical notes field for documentation
   - Workflow integration: Appears in EHR discharge workflow
   
   For Care Managers:
   - Follow-up schedule and patient contact log
   - Compliance tracking (% completing recommended interventions)
   - Patient contact notes
   - Readmission outcomes (did patient readmit?)
   
   For Hospital Leadership:
   - Monthly dashboard showing:
     * Readmission rate by risk tier (validation of model)
     * Readmission rate trend (is it improving?)
     * Intervention adherence rates
     * Cost-benefit summary ($X spent on interventions, $Y saved from prevented readmissions)
   - Comparison vs. previous period / vs. benchmark hospitals

E) Monitoring & Continuous Improvement
   - Monthly model performance validation
