6. RISK MANAGEMENT
=============================================================================

RISK 1: Model Performance Variation
Risk: Model predicts well on development data but poorly on hospital's patients
Mitigation:
- Validate on hospital's own recent discharges
- Recalibrate if needed (hospital-specific readmission rates vary)
- Monitor monthly: Plot actual vs. predicted readmission rates
- If performance degrades: Retrain model with new data

RISK 2: Clinical Staff Resistance
Risk: Discharge planners ignore system recommendations; "I know my patients"
Mitigation:
- Early engagement: Interview staff, incorporate feedback
- Training: Explain evidence base (75% AUC, published validation)
- Autonomy: System is ADVISORY; clinicians make final decisions
- Feedback: Show staff that high-risk predictions correct
- Champions: Identify early adopters; have them mentor skeptics

RISK 3: Workflow Disruption
Risk: System adds burden to discharge process; slows discharges
Mitigation:
- Lean workflow design: Minimize additional steps
- Automation: Pre-populate checklists based on risk tier
- Integration: Embed in EHR (not separate tool)
- Training: Discharge planners know exactly what to do
- Monitoring: Track discharge times (should NOT increase)

RISK 4: Intervention Intensity Mismatch
Risk: Intensive interventions too burdensome; low adherence
Or: Intensive interventions insufficient; high-risk patients still readmit
Mitigation:
- Pilot testing: Validate protocols work
- Feedback loops: Adjust intensity based on outcomes & staff feedback
- Flexibility: Allow clinician discretion (modify protocol if clinically indicated)
- Evidence: Interventions based on published literature

RISK 5: Data Privacy & Compliance
Risk: Patient data exposed; HIPAA violation
Mitigation:
- Secure cloud hosting (HIPAA-compliant AWS/Azure/Google Cloud)
- Encryption: At-rest and in-transit
- Access controls: Role-based (only authorized staff see data)
- Audit trails: Log all system access
- Compliance review: Annual security assessment

RISK 6: Cost Overrun
Risk: System costs more than $750K; ROI negative
Mitigation:
- Phased implementation: Start with single hospital, then expand
- Vendor selection: Competitive bidding
- Project management: Track spending, enforce budget
- Alternative: Use open-source tools (R packages, Shiny dashboards) to reduce licensing costs

